#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:145
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Wireplumber"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:147
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:150
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"In order for Wireplumber to be used by Pipewire, Wireplumber and Pipewire "
"must be configured to start when a desktop environment is started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:156
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Pipewire now provides it's own Pulseaudio server implementation, which "
"causes runtime conflicts with the server provided by Pulseaudio itself.  "
"This generally presents itself by applications hanging or malfunctioning "
"when trying to play or record audio and video. First, prevent Pulseaudio "
"from starting it's own server implementation by running the following "
"commands as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:164
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>rm -vf /etc/xdg/autostart/pulseaudio.desktop         &amp;&amp;\n"
"rm -vf /etc/xdg/Xwayland-session.d/00-pulseaudio-x11 &amp;&amp;\n"
"sed -e '$a autospawn = no' -i /etc/pulse/client.conf</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:169
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, configure Wireplumber to start when a desktop environment is started. "
"Run the following commands as the &root; user to enable the systemd user "
"units:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:174
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>systemctl enable --global pipewire.socket       &amp;&amp;\n"
"systemctl enable --global pipewire-pulse.socket &amp;&amp;\n"
"systemctl enable --global wireplumber</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:179
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Next, create a shell script that will start Wireplumber and Pipewire in the "
"correct order as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:183
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>#!/bin/sh\n"
"# Begin /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh\n"
"\n"
"# First, kill any previous instances of pipewire, wireplumber, or pipewire-pulse\n"
"# that are running. Multiple instances of the daemon can not be run at the same\n"
"# time, and this helps prevent possible errors if a user logs out or logs in\n"
"# too fast, and restores audio if Pipewire hangs and needs to be reset.\n"
"\n"
"pkill -u ${USER} -fx /usr/bin/pipewire-pulse\n"
"pkill -u ${USER} -fx /usr/bin/wireplumber\n"
"pkill -u ${USER} -fx /usr/bin/pipewire\n"
"\n"
"# Start Pipewire first.\n"
"exec /usr/bin/pipewire &amp;\n"
"\n"
"# Next, we need to wait until pipewire is up before starting wireplumber.\n"
"# This prevents a possible race condition where pipewire takes too long\n"
"# to start, as some users have run into.\n"
"while [ $(pgrep -f /usr/bin/pipewire) = \"\" ]; do\n"
"   sleep 1\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"# Start Wireplumber now that Pipewire has been started.\n"
"exec /usr/bin/wireplumber &amp;\n"
"\n"
"# Start the Pulseaudio server included with Pipewire.\n"
"exec /usr/bin/pipewire-pulse &amp;\n"
"\n"
"# End /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:216
#, xml-text
msgid "Next, make this shell script executable as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:219
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>chmod +x /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:222
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Finally, create an XDG Autostart file that will run "
"<command>/usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh</command> when a desktop environment "
"is started, as the &root; user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:227
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/xdg/autostart/pipewire.desktop &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Version=1.0\n"
"Name=Pipewire\n"
"Comment=Starts the Pipewire and Wireplumber daemons\n"
"Exec=/usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh\n"
"Terminal=false\n"
"Type=Application</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/multimedia/libdriv/wireplumber.xml:238
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now that Wireplumber is configured to start when a desktop environment is "
"started, it is recommended that you log out of your session and log back in "
"again."
msgstr ""

